WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.154 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.829 --> 00:39.373
Then is it okay if I like you?

00:39.957 --> 00:41.792
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

00:42.876 --> 00:44.795
[stammers]

00:47.589 --> 00:50.425
[heartbeats echoing]

01:02.938 --> 01:04.064
Uh…

01:04.147 --> 01:07.359
-I think we should turn this off.
-[clicks]

01:08.944 --> 01:11.905
[stutters] I didn't mean that…

01:11.989 --> 01:14.366
I didn't mean that, either.

01:14.449 --> 01:18.245
My grandmother kept talking
about us dating,

01:19.413 --> 01:20.706
so I was just…

01:21.540 --> 01:25.085
trying to stop that in advance
since you might feel uneasy.

01:25.669 --> 01:26.670
That's all.

01:27.254 --> 01:29.006
That's really it?

01:30.716 --> 01:32.050
[mumbles]

01:34.553 --> 01:35.971
Should there be something else?

01:38.348 --> 01:39.641
[♪ music fades]

01:39.725 --> 01:41.184
I'll start driving, then.

01:45.397 --> 01:46.398
EPISODE 5

01:46.481 --> 01:47.482
GYEONGJU

01:47.566 --> 01:50.777
[reporter over radio] The cold is expected
to arrive earlier this year than usual.

01:50.861 --> 01:54.573
The first snow may fall sooner
than average as well.

01:54.656 --> 01:56.658
The continental high-pressure system--

02:00.704 --> 02:01.705
[Chan sighs]

02:03.290 --> 02:05.334
It would be a shame to just leave.

02:06.835 --> 02:08.503
Can you pull over?

02:11.465 --> 02:13.467
[water gushing]

02:15.344 --> 02:16.887
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

02:20.807 --> 02:24.311
Wow. It would've been a huge shame
if we'd just left.

02:29.191 --> 02:30.192
I hate snow.

02:31.401 --> 02:32.944
Especially the first snow.

02:34.404 --> 02:35.697
The first snow?

02:35.781 --> 02:37.783
Remember what I told you about my parents?

02:38.367 --> 02:42.204
The accident happened
on the first snowfall.

02:43.372 --> 02:46.333
So it became an unlucky day for me.

02:47.626 --> 02:48.877
Mmm.

02:48.960 --> 02:50.796
I know it's a lame jinx, though.

02:54.633 --> 02:55.676
[sniffles]

02:55.759 --> 02:56.802
[Chan groans]

02:56.885 --> 03:00.931
Then I'll start hating
the first snow, too.

03:03.767 --> 03:04.935
Oh, um…

03:05.018 --> 03:07.562
I have a habit of copying other people.

03:12.609 --> 03:14.945
I'm not sure if it's okay to ask this,

03:16.488 --> 03:20.742
but when I talked about my mom's voice…

03:21.952 --> 03:24.413
you said there's someone you miss.

03:25.288 --> 03:26.581
That was your mother, right?

03:29.334 --> 03:31.044
Your grandmother told me.

03:32.754 --> 03:36.216
I was surprised when you spoke
like you experienced the same thing.

03:40.262 --> 03:42.764
Uh…

03:43.849 --> 03:44.850
Croissant.

03:44.933 --> 03:46.393
Croissant?

03:47.936 --> 03:49.146
The pastry?

03:50.355 --> 03:51.731
The crescent moon.

03:53.400 --> 03:54.943
It's "croissant" in French.

03:55.610 --> 03:59.531
Don't you crave croissants
when you see the crescent moon?

04:00.657 --> 04:01.658
[stutters]

04:02.701 --> 04:04.536
Anyway, your grandmother said--

04:04.619 --> 04:05.954
What about the half-moon?

04:07.038 --> 04:08.748
Omurice!

04:08.832 --> 04:09.833
And the full moon?

04:09.916 --> 04:12.169
It's pizza. Huh?

04:13.378 --> 04:15.589
Was it just me, then? [chuckles]

04:17.048 --> 04:18.717
I'm craving pizza.

04:19.968 --> 04:21.970
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

04:29.728 --> 04:32.105
Ben, we're here.

04:33.482 --> 04:35.692
[inhales sharply] Are they not here yet?

04:37.944 --> 04:39.988
[Ben and team in English] Surprise!

04:40.071 --> 04:42.157
[cheering, exclaiming]

04:43.533 --> 04:45.327
-How have you been?
-I'm good, I'm good.

04:45.410 --> 04:47.746
-It's great to see you here in Korea.
-Me too.

04:47.829 --> 04:49.498
Let me quickly introduce her.

04:49.581 --> 04:51.958
Guys, this is designer Haran Song.

04:52.542 --> 04:55.420
[in Korean] Uh… Nice to meet you.

04:55.504 --> 04:59.049
[hesitates] I'm Peter. Uh…

04:59.132 --> 05:01.426
-[in English] It's so great to meet you.
-Hi, nice to meet you.

05:01.510 --> 05:03.261
-This is my team.
-Nice to meet you. Hi.

05:03.345 --> 05:04.346
Nice to meet you.

05:04.429 --> 05:06.890
We're going to spend the morning
taking in the scenery,

05:06.973 --> 05:08.683
visiting some historic sites,

05:08.767 --> 05:11.436
and then we will head over
to Yangdong Village.

05:11.520 --> 05:16.441
So on page 3, there's more information
about Yangdong Village.

05:16.525 --> 05:21.363
So as you can see, there's a big tree.
This tree is more than 500 years old.

05:21.446 --> 05:23.698
It's really famous.

05:23.782 --> 05:26.576
[Chan's grandma in Korean]
So his father sent him to America,

05:26.660 --> 05:29.663
and he suffered there.

05:30.247 --> 05:31.748
[Haran] "Something terrible"?

05:31.832 --> 05:34.167
-What happened in the US?
-[♪ soft emotional music playing]

05:34.751 --> 05:37.462
Why won't he tell me about himself?

05:37.546 --> 05:39.089
[Peter in English] That's a great idea.
Let's use that tree.

05:39.172 --> 05:40.382
It's famous in Yangdong.

05:40.465 --> 05:43.593
[Ben in Korean] Ms. Song,
about the materials you sent over…

05:43.677 --> 05:44.719
[Haran] Yes.

05:44.803 --> 05:47.264
It's pretty decorative, right?

05:47.347 --> 05:48.640
We'll turn it into a pattern.

05:48.723 --> 05:52.185
Why am I someone you shouldn't like?

05:52.269 --> 05:54.271
[♪ music continuing]

05:55.063 --> 05:57.065
[indistinct chatter]

06:03.530 --> 06:05.574
[wind whooshing]

06:05.657 --> 06:07.367
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

06:07.450 --> 06:08.451
[♪ music fades]

06:08.535 --> 06:10.453
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

06:10.537 --> 06:12.372
[lively chatter]

06:12.455 --> 06:14.082
-[group cheering]
-[Chan] Oh?

06:16.001 --> 06:18.003
-[sighs]
-What are you doing?

06:18.086 --> 06:20.046
Oh. Playing a game to pick the driver.

06:20.130 --> 06:21.840
You saw our team, right?

06:21.923 --> 06:23.300
They're all mischievous.

06:23.383 --> 06:24.384
[laughter]

06:24.467 --> 06:25.844
Did you lose?

06:25.927 --> 06:28.013
-Then I'll drive--
-I'm the king of games.

06:28.763 --> 06:30.807
I won, of course. [chuckles softly]

06:31.683 --> 06:32.851
We're here!

06:32.934 --> 06:34.144
Hey, Sol!

06:34.227 --> 06:35.604
Why are you alone?

06:35.687 --> 06:37.606
Raemee is here!

06:37.689 --> 06:40.942
Gosh, I just realized on the way here
how beautiful Gyeongju is.

06:41.026 --> 06:42.193
It's totally my style.

06:42.277 --> 06:46.031
It seems like
you're moving here. [chuckles]

06:46.114 --> 06:49.576
I need this much luggage
at least to dress for the occasion.

06:49.659 --> 06:52.162
-Don't play dumb!
-[chuckles]

06:52.245 --> 06:54.664
-We're here, too.
-Me too.

06:55.582 --> 06:58.710
[in English] Okay, everybody's here.
We'll leave in 10 minutes. Okay, guys?

06:58.793 --> 07:00.795
[♪ uplifting song playing]

07:05.133 --> 07:06.801
[lively chatter, laughter]

07:08.678 --> 07:09.971
[in Korean] Let's lie down!

07:10.055 --> 07:11.389
[all sigh contentedly]

07:13.058 --> 07:14.726
[Sol] This is so nice.

07:35.413 --> 07:36.831
HWANGNIDAN STREET
GYEONGJU BREAD

07:36.915 --> 07:38.917
[♪ song continues]

08:16.538 --> 08:18.081
[Sol exclaims in awe]

08:18.164 --> 08:19.666
[employees talking indistinctly]

08:24.337 --> 08:26.339
[indistinct conversation continues]

08:32.429 --> 08:33.430
-[inhales sharply]
-[Sol exclaims]

08:33.513 --> 08:34.848
[mumbles]

08:35.598 --> 08:36.599
Yes, Ms. Kim.

08:37.058 --> 08:38.059
Seeing it in person,

08:38.143 --> 08:40.937
I think we should emphasize
the Korean elements a bit more.

08:42.355 --> 08:45.817
Then I'll come up with another sketch
with that in mind.

08:46.526 --> 08:47.736
All right.

08:48.653 --> 08:49.654
[line disconnects]

08:50.613 --> 08:53.324
[sighs heavily] This is pretty tough.

08:56.745 --> 08:59.664
Aren't you tired?
It's a tough schedule, isn't it?

08:59.748 --> 09:01.249
It's okay. [chuckles]

09:02.584 --> 09:04.294
Everyone seems excited, though.

09:04.377 --> 09:06.921
You seem like friends
rather than colleagues.

09:07.005 --> 09:10.925
We weren't this close,
but after Too Much joined us… [exclaims]

09:11.009 --> 09:12.343
[both laugh]

09:12.427 --> 09:13.928
You didn't join at the same time?

09:14.012 --> 09:17.182
Too Much is several years my junior.
At school and at work.

09:17.265 --> 09:18.850
He joined this field pretty late.

09:19.809 --> 09:23.229
Oh. Then he studied something else
before animation?

09:23.313 --> 09:25.398
[sighs] I don't know, either.

09:25.482 --> 09:30.278
He never tells me
what he did before entering CalArts.

09:31.196 --> 09:33.114
[in English] It's like he erased it.

09:34.491 --> 09:36.701
[in Korean] Erasing his time…

09:39.120 --> 09:40.455
Are you two badmouthing me?

09:40.538 --> 09:42.207
[laughing] You caught us!

09:42.290 --> 09:43.792
I'm fleeing!

09:44.793 --> 09:46.211
You badmouthed me, didn't you?

09:46.294 --> 09:48.129
-No, we didn't.
-I think you did.

09:49.297 --> 09:50.799
Did you sketch something?

09:50.882 --> 09:53.009
-Oh… Yes. Do you want to see?
-Sure.

09:56.471 --> 09:57.472
[Haran exclaims]

09:58.807 --> 09:59.808
Wow.

09:59.891 --> 10:02.435
Your grandmother said
you didn't draw for a while.

10:03.103 --> 10:05.396
How did you end up drawing again?

10:05.480 --> 10:06.648
I'm curious.

10:06.731 --> 10:08.233
Was there a special reason?

10:09.109 --> 10:10.860
Oh. Hmm…

10:12.362 --> 10:15.115
[♪ sentimental music playing]

10:15.198 --> 10:16.199
I'd like a ticket

10:16.866 --> 10:19.828
for the earliest departure anywhere
except the US.

10:19.911 --> 10:21.871
[in English] Hi, where are you from?

10:22.789 --> 10:25.792
Well, anyway… Enjoy Florence.

10:36.469 --> 10:39.305
THINGS TO GET RID OF: THE PAST
THINGS TO DO FROM NOW ON

10:42.142 --> 10:44.769
THINGS I WANT TO DO FROM NOW ON

10:46.813 --> 10:49.732
DRAW

10:51.276 --> 10:52.652
[Chan in Korean] I just…

10:52.735 --> 10:53.736
[sighs]

10:54.737 --> 10:56.489
didn't want to live like a corpse.

10:57.740 --> 10:58.741
A corpse?

10:59.951 --> 11:02.871
Doesn't it feel like we time-traveled?

11:03.371 --> 11:06.291
This tree is over 500 years old.

11:06.374 --> 11:07.375
Mmm.

11:08.751 --> 11:10.753
[♪ music continues]

11:19.637 --> 11:23.016
If you can time travel,
when do you want to return to?

11:23.099 --> 11:24.934
Mmm… I don't want to go back.

11:25.018 --> 11:26.144
[♪ music fades]

11:26.227 --> 11:30.148
I don't have a past I want to return to.

11:31.608 --> 11:33.943
Doesn't everyone have
a certain moment, though?

11:35.570 --> 11:37.155
You never know when you'll die.

11:37.947 --> 11:41.409
You should enjoy your life
instead of regretting the past,

11:41.492 --> 11:42.869
so you won't feel upset later.

11:44.495 --> 11:45.830
[♪ pleasant music playing]

11:45.914 --> 11:47.123
Mmm.

11:47.207 --> 11:49.334
Maybe it's that free trial.

11:49.417 --> 11:51.252
I do feel kind of excited these days.

11:51.961 --> 11:55.089
We went to the Hangang River,
made pottery,

11:56.049 --> 11:57.175
and came here.

11:59.594 --> 12:01.512
You're doing great.

12:01.596 --> 12:05.725
Keep enjoying your life
like this every day,

12:06.684 --> 12:07.685
even when…

12:08.603 --> 12:09.812
I'm not here later.

12:31.751 --> 12:33.962
-[♪ music fades]
-[elevator dings]

12:36.464 --> 12:38.925
Oh? You changed your outfit.

12:39.008 --> 12:41.844
You weren't wearing that earlier.
Why did you change?

12:43.054 --> 12:46.391
Oh… I just bought it
while doing some trend research.

12:46.474 --> 12:50.061
That's strange.
It really isn't your style.

12:50.144 --> 12:52.230
It looks like
you picked it out in a hurry.

12:52.313 --> 12:54.148
Did I miss some kind of new trend?

12:54.232 --> 12:55.566
-Or--
-Shut up.

12:55.650 --> 12:57.485
You're so talkative.

12:57.568 --> 12:58.653
[groans cutely]

12:58.736 --> 13:01.072
I'm just curious about you.

13:01.155 --> 13:03.491
This is my way
of expressing love and affection.

13:08.246 --> 13:09.747
[♪ amusing music playing]

13:09.831 --> 13:12.250
[Hayeong] I'll just go meet Cha Min.

13:21.342 --> 13:23.011
What's this awkward silence?

13:23.094 --> 13:25.430
Say something, Hayeong.

13:25.513 --> 13:28.558
You're usually talkative.
It'll seem like he's making you nervous.

13:28.641 --> 13:31.894
Just tease him or something,
like you usually do.

13:32.437 --> 13:33.438
[♪ music fades]

13:33.521 --> 13:35.940
-Is there something wrong?
-What?

13:36.024 --> 13:38.192
You seem quieter than usual.

13:38.276 --> 13:39.569
Do you think

13:39.652 --> 13:44.073
I'm always…
[stuttering] just chatting loudly?

13:44.157 --> 13:45.575
That's not what I meant.

13:46.451 --> 13:47.452
Sorry.

13:48.745 --> 13:51.080
But aren't you getting off?

13:51.164 --> 13:52.874
Right. I am.

13:52.957 --> 13:55.418
-[thuds]
-[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

13:55.501 --> 13:56.753
Be careful.

13:59.547 --> 14:00.548
[clears throat]

14:03.676 --> 14:04.677
[♪ music fades]

14:05.136 --> 14:06.137
[grunts]

14:08.765 --> 14:09.766
[sighs heavily]

14:18.775 --> 14:20.777
[♪ melancholy music playing]

14:24.864 --> 14:27.116
[cell phone vibrating]

14:32.330 --> 14:33.372
Hey, Manjae.

14:33.456 --> 14:35.333
Did you move or something?

14:35.416 --> 14:38.711
You said you'd drop by sometime,
but you never came.

14:38.795 --> 14:42.048
Sorry, I've been pretty busy.

14:42.131 --> 14:44.509
Why don't I drop by after work today?

14:44.592 --> 14:46.469
Sure. Come and see Genius, too.

14:48.429 --> 14:49.430
[Manjae chuckles]

14:49.931 --> 14:51.307
Okay. I'll see you later.

15:05.488 --> 15:06.864
[sighs]

15:06.948 --> 15:07.949
[♪ music fades]

15:10.952 --> 15:11.953
[brakes hiss]

15:14.997 --> 15:16.833
Hey, it's Yougyum.

15:17.333 --> 15:18.376
What?

15:18.876 --> 15:20.878
He just came out of a jewelry shop.

15:20.962 --> 15:23.214
I bet he bought matching rings.

15:23.881 --> 15:24.966
You're so lucky, Hadam.

15:31.055 --> 15:32.640
Matching rings?

15:32.723 --> 15:34.433
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

15:35.685 --> 15:36.686
[chuckles softly]

15:37.854 --> 15:40.565
[employees] Thank you for the food!

15:40.648 --> 15:42.900
[indistinct chatter]

15:47.780 --> 15:49.448
[in English] Try this one, try this one.

15:53.119 --> 15:55.496
[Raemee in Korean] Yummy. This is amazing.

15:57.582 --> 15:58.666
I'll eat those for you.

15:58.749 --> 16:01.085
The snot and neon aliens.

16:01.878 --> 16:02.879
Thanks. [chuckles]

16:04.130 --> 16:07.175
[in English] Don't you guys think that
Yangdong Village was just so gorgeous?

16:07.258 --> 16:09.468
It was really unique, don't you think?

16:09.552 --> 16:11.971
I totally agree.
It kind of felt like it was timeless.

16:12.054 --> 16:15.141
Actually, I think it feels
even better than the photo. Right?

16:15.224 --> 16:16.976
[female guest] Yeah, it's so beautiful.

16:17.059 --> 16:20.396
But do you know the scene
where Won first goes back to the past?

16:22.231 --> 16:27.403
Uh… Maybe we can make that moment
a little bit deeper. Do you guys agree?

16:27.486 --> 16:30.239
[Ben] Maybe that's exactly
what we should do, yeah.

16:30.323 --> 16:31.324
[male guest] Awesome.

16:31.407 --> 16:33.284
-Okay, then… Mmm.
-[Ben] Let's do it.

16:33.367 --> 16:35.494
-Thank you so much. Let's just eat first.
-[laughter]

16:35.578 --> 16:37.371
[in Korean] All together. One, two, three!

16:37.455 --> 16:40.208
[all] The ocean!

16:40.291 --> 16:42.293
[♪ upbeat music playing]

16:44.378 --> 16:46.380
[yelling, exclaiming]

16:47.924 --> 16:49.342
[laughter]

16:50.092 --> 16:52.220
Wait!

16:52.303 --> 16:54.180
No, wait! Hey, Raemee!

17:00.269 --> 17:02.271
[indistinct chatter]

17:09.195 --> 17:11.197
-[hums in thought, speaks indistinctly]
-[inhales sharply]

17:13.699 --> 17:15.701
[waves crashing]

17:16.327 --> 17:17.328
[♪ music ends]

17:31.884 --> 17:32.885
[Haran sighs wearily]

17:32.969 --> 17:35.096
I can't even decide on a concept.

17:36.722 --> 17:38.516
You there, who's mulling over pens.

17:39.392 --> 17:42.478
Do you want to go see the sea cave
to clear your head?

17:42.562 --> 17:43.604
[chuckles softly]

17:43.688 --> 17:45.147
[in English] Nice timing.

17:45.231 --> 17:47.149
[in Korean] I needed
a reason to take a break.

17:47.233 --> 17:48.568
[chuckles]

17:51.779 --> 17:52.822
Oh, right.

17:55.116 --> 17:56.867
I never told you that, though.

17:58.411 --> 18:00.204
I told you I don't eat oysters,

18:00.288 --> 18:03.291
but I never told you
eggplants seemed like neon aliens.

18:04.750 --> 18:05.835
[Chan] I'll eat those for you.

18:05.918 --> 18:07.878
The snot and neon aliens.

18:07.962 --> 18:09.714
[Haran] It's neon-colored. Yuck!

18:09.797 --> 18:12.049
The taste of a neon alien. [retches]

18:12.133 --> 18:14.135
[♪ mysterious music playing]

18:14.844 --> 18:15.845
Uh…

18:20.016 --> 18:22.268
No, how else would you know?

18:22.351 --> 18:23.394
I guess I told you.

18:24.103 --> 18:25.605
Sorry, I must've forgotten.

18:25.688 --> 18:26.689
Is it this way?

18:26.772 --> 18:27.982
-[♪ music fades]
-[Haran chuckles]

18:38.784 --> 18:40.786
[waves crashing]

18:42.538 --> 18:43.539
What are you doing?

18:48.753 --> 18:51.797
Don't you want to ride a plane
when you see a vapor trail?

18:53.633 --> 18:55.635
I actually rode one after seeing one.

18:56.927 --> 19:00.264
I went to meet the person
who gave me that fountain pen I lost.

19:02.099 --> 19:04.060
I used to work at a different company,

19:04.685 --> 19:09.231
and he was the brother of my team leader
who really cared for me.

19:10.232 --> 19:13.819
But soon after we started dating,
he went to Boston to study.

19:13.903 --> 19:15.821
[♪ dramatic music playing]

19:17.073 --> 19:18.240
[Hyeokchan] Nice to meet you.

19:18.324 --> 19:20.451
I'm Kang Hyeokchan.

19:20.534 --> 19:21.869
I'm glad you're Korean, too.

19:21.952 --> 19:23.120
I hope we get along.

19:25.289 --> 19:26.332
[breathing heavily]

19:27.041 --> 19:28.250
Are you okay?

19:28.918 --> 19:30.920
[metallic clink echoing]

19:33.714 --> 19:36.050
Are you all right? You've gone pale.

19:37.176 --> 19:38.511
[inhales sharply]

19:38.594 --> 19:40.846
-If I'm not okay, will you carry me?
-[♪ music fades]

19:41.555 --> 19:43.474
Are you seriously joking right now?

19:43.557 --> 19:45.142
Are you sure you're okay?

19:46.519 --> 19:48.312
I'll be okay.

19:49.563 --> 19:51.273
It's all going to be okay.

19:51.357 --> 19:52.942
[♪ solemn music playing]

20:00.574 --> 20:01.575
[♪ music fades]

20:01.659 --> 20:03.911
-Yougyum!
-Hey, Hadam.

20:06.372 --> 20:09.667
My academy ends at 9:00 p.m.
Should we meet after?

20:09.750 --> 20:11.043
What?

20:11.127 --> 20:13.045
Did we plan to meet today?

20:13.629 --> 20:14.797
Mmm…

20:14.880 --> 20:19.051
No, but I think you have a reason
to meet me later.

20:19.135 --> 20:20.261
I don't.

20:20.928 --> 20:23.848
Why don't you spend some time
with your grandma--

20:23.931 --> 20:26.517
Why are you suddenly
bringing up my grandma?

20:26.600 --> 20:27.727
What?

20:27.810 --> 20:29.145
[♪ whimsical music playing]

20:29.228 --> 20:31.313
Oh… Well…

20:31.397 --> 20:32.857
Hey, Changmo!

20:32.940 --> 20:36.026
I have something urgent
to discuss with Changmo, so I have to go.

20:36.110 --> 20:37.570
Hey, Changmo!

20:39.405 --> 20:42.908
What? Changmo isn't even there.
[hums excitedly]

20:43.784 --> 20:46.287
[scoffs] He should hurry up
and give me the ring.

20:47.663 --> 20:51.333
Unfortunately, it seems like
he gave the ring to Han Sora.

20:51.417 --> 20:52.418
[♪ music fades]

20:52.501 --> 20:54.545
She didn't have that a few days ago.

20:54.628 --> 20:56.130
But she was wearing this
in her recent feed.

20:57.298 --> 20:59.258
[scoffs] Don't be ridiculous.

21:00.050 --> 21:02.803
If a girl group trainee with her looks
hits on him,

21:02.887 --> 21:04.722
he could easily fall for her.

21:09.518 --> 21:11.520
[♪ whimsical music playing]

21:14.482 --> 21:16.567
[sighs] That's nonsense.

21:18.402 --> 21:19.403
[♪ music ends]

21:19.487 --> 21:20.488
GUARDIAN

21:20.571 --> 21:22.364
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

21:23.240 --> 21:24.408
[Manjae chuckles]

21:25.409 --> 21:27.203
I wanted to give you this.

21:27.286 --> 21:31.540
It finally found its owner
after over 50 years.

21:31.624 --> 21:32.708
[chuckles]

21:36.045 --> 21:38.255
What? "La Vie en rose"?

21:39.173 --> 21:41.550
-This is my favorite song.
-[chuckles]

21:41.634 --> 21:44.178
But what did you mean
by this finding its owner?

21:44.261 --> 21:47.890
You were humming that song all the time
when we lived in Chuncheon.

21:47.973 --> 21:50.726
-I played it with the harmonica, too.
-[gasps]

21:50.810 --> 21:51.894
Right.

21:52.478 --> 21:53.479
I remember.

21:53.562 --> 21:55.231
After I went to college in Seoul

21:55.314 --> 21:58.651
and heard you got accepted
to a medical school the next year,

21:58.734 --> 22:01.570
I went to Chuncheon to give you this.

22:01.654 --> 22:04.323
I waited by the tree
where we always hung out,

22:04.406 --> 22:07.243
but you never showed.

22:07.326 --> 22:08.410
You waited for me?

22:08.494 --> 22:12.665
It snowed like crazy that day.

22:12.748 --> 22:15.584
I almost became a snowman
waiting for you there.

22:15.668 --> 22:16.669
[both laugh]

22:16.752 --> 22:20.422
I only heard the news later on.

22:20.506 --> 22:23.717
The news that I ran off with my tuition
and hopped on a flight to Paris?

22:23.801 --> 22:25.636
Yes! [laughs]

22:25.719 --> 22:29.640
I didn't get to give you this record,
so I just listened to it.

22:29.723 --> 22:32.184
[gasps softly] It was so nice.

22:32.268 --> 22:35.312
That's how I got obsessed
and started collecting vinyls.

22:36.188 --> 22:38.065
And this is the result.

22:38.148 --> 22:41.819
It's all your fault, Kim Nabong.

22:41.902 --> 22:43.404
[laughs]

22:44.822 --> 22:46.073
Is that so?

22:47.992 --> 22:48.993
[sighs]

22:49.952 --> 22:53.205
We were dazzling back then.

22:56.959 --> 22:58.210
It's nice seeing you again.

22:59.378 --> 23:02.464
I'd been so busy pushing forward
that I'd forgotten about our old hometown.

23:03.674 --> 23:05.009
I agree.

23:05.092 --> 23:06.176
[both laugh]

23:06.260 --> 23:08.304
Instead of just reminiscing,

23:08.387 --> 23:11.015
why don't we visit Chuncheon sometime?

23:11.098 --> 23:12.099
Chuncheon?

23:12.182 --> 23:14.935
Aren't you curious
whether that tree is still there

23:15.436 --> 23:18.230
and how much our neighborhood has changed?

23:18.314 --> 23:19.565
[gasps]

23:19.648 --> 23:20.983
Right.

23:21.775 --> 23:23.485
All right, let's go there sometime.

23:23.569 --> 23:25.279
Okay. Let's do that.

23:25.696 --> 23:27.698
[both laughing]

23:31.493 --> 23:33.495
[indistinct chatter]

23:38.417 --> 23:39.752
-[chatter continues]
-[sighs softly]

23:39.835 --> 23:41.170
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

23:41.962 --> 23:44.882
[Chan] Lab, glass tube, blood…

23:45.591 --> 23:46.675
Whose blood?

23:47.343 --> 23:48.469
[sighs]

23:49.136 --> 23:50.471
Yes, Ms. Kim.

23:51.263 --> 23:53.474
Je Raemee sent his design?

23:55.142 --> 23:57.269
Oh. Sorry, I haven't
sketched anything yet.

23:59.355 --> 24:01.774
[doctor] If you don't want to suffer again
because of your past,

24:01.857 --> 24:04.193
it would be best
to keep a distance from her.

24:05.277 --> 24:06.779
[Chan] Did something else happen

24:07.696 --> 24:09.406
besides the explosion?

24:10.950 --> 24:13.035
[groans] Hurry up. Why are you so slow?

24:13.118 --> 24:14.536
-Sorry.
-[♪ music fades]

24:14.620 --> 24:17.206
[in English] All right, everybody.
Let's head back and get some rest.

24:17.289 --> 24:18.499
Yeah, let's go.

24:18.582 --> 24:20.584
[Sol in Korean] We'll see you later.

24:20.668 --> 24:22.252
[indistinct chatter]

24:22.962 --> 24:24.755
Oh? Where's Ms. Song?

24:25.589 --> 24:28.676
-Huh?
-What? Weren't you with her?

24:29.426 --> 24:31.095
You were hanging out the whole time.

24:31.178 --> 24:34.306
She said she forgot her scarf.
She went to get it.

24:34.390 --> 24:36.642
Goodness. She's a klutz sometimes.

24:36.725 --> 24:38.602
[leaves rustling]

24:42.481 --> 24:44.441
[thunder rumbling]

24:44.525 --> 24:45.526
Oh, uh…

24:45.985 --> 24:47.695
I'll go and get her. You go ahead.

24:47.778 --> 24:49.238
[♪ tense music playing]

24:55.536 --> 24:56.704
Ms. Song!

24:57.746 --> 24:58.872
Ms. Song!

24:59.623 --> 25:00.916
[pants]

25:01.000 --> 25:02.626
Song Haran! [sighs]

25:02.710 --> 25:03.877
[Haran whimpers]

25:03.961 --> 25:05.546
[pants]

25:05.629 --> 25:06.672
-Oh?
-[♪ music ends]

25:06.755 --> 25:07.756
Why were you--

25:07.840 --> 25:09.091
[panting] Why are you so fast?

25:09.174 --> 25:11.385
I… [pants]

25:11.969 --> 25:13.721
I thought I'd left this here,

25:13.804 --> 25:15.764
but I found it in my pocket
and headed down.

25:15.848 --> 25:17.516
But then I heard you went to find me.

25:17.599 --> 25:20.144
I kept calling, but you wouldn't answer.

25:20.227 --> 25:21.979
[grunts] I'm sorry.

25:22.396 --> 25:24.064
I guess I didn't hear it over the rain.

25:24.148 --> 25:26.066
I should've been more careful.

25:26.150 --> 25:27.651
You're always apologizing.

25:27.735 --> 25:29.278
-Let's go.
-Okay.

25:29.361 --> 25:30.571
[thunderclap]

25:30.654 --> 25:32.156
[both exclaim nervously]

25:32.781 --> 25:34.283
-[exclaims frantically]
-[grunts]

25:35.534 --> 25:37.244
-[exclaims]
-Let's get out of the rain.

25:37.327 --> 25:38.954
-Over there.
-[Haran exclaims, squeals]

25:44.084 --> 25:45.502
Sit down.

25:46.295 --> 25:48.505
Oh. Thanks. [sighs]

25:49.006 --> 25:50.007
[groans]

25:50.090 --> 25:51.633
Are you hurt?

25:51.717 --> 25:53.302
No, it's nothing. [chuckles awkwardly]

25:53.385 --> 25:55.471
-[rain pattering]
-[Chan sighs wearily]

25:55.971 --> 25:58.599
You shouldn't climb
with your shoelaces so loose.

26:00.350 --> 26:01.727
Your feet must have hurt a lot.

26:01.810 --> 26:03.562
-Hey, it's dirty.
-[grunts]

26:04.563 --> 26:06.356
Tell me if it keeps hurting.

26:06.982 --> 26:08.692
I'll carry you if I have to.

26:11.612 --> 26:13.614
[♪ melancholy music playing]

26:14.907 --> 26:16.784
I can't hear on this side.

26:16.867 --> 26:17.868
[gasps lightly]

26:17.951 --> 26:20.704
[Chan's grandma]
So his father sent him to America,

26:20.788 --> 26:23.957
and he suffered there.

26:25.417 --> 26:26.418
[sighs]

26:27.294 --> 26:28.796
To be honest, I'm curious.

26:29.546 --> 26:30.839
About what?

26:31.423 --> 26:33.967
About what I heard from your grandmother.

26:35.094 --> 26:38.013
I want to know what happened in America,

26:39.389 --> 26:42.601
what you meant by being trapped in winter,

26:42.684 --> 26:45.104
and who freed you from it.

26:45.729 --> 26:48.649
I'm getting more comfortable around you,

26:49.316 --> 26:51.860
and I've been telling you
things about myself,

26:51.944 --> 26:53.278
but…

26:54.113 --> 26:56.615
you don't seem to be telling me
much about yourself.

27:02.704 --> 27:03.705
[♪ music fades]

27:04.456 --> 27:06.875
I started studying animation
six years ago.

27:07.584 --> 27:10.295
I worked my butt off and graduated early

27:10.379 --> 27:13.340
then entered my current company
as a character designer.

27:13.423 --> 27:15.843
I became a supervisor by luck

27:15.926 --> 27:18.470
since Won was a Korean character.

27:20.222 --> 27:23.433
[grunts] I commute by bike

27:24.142 --> 27:27.062
since the office
is a 10-minute ride from home.

27:27.145 --> 27:29.273
You met my teammates, right?

27:29.356 --> 27:30.482
Everyone's really close.

27:31.191 --> 27:32.359
-And--
-Wait.

27:34.194 --> 27:36.363
-What are you talking about?
-I'm sorry,

27:38.115 --> 27:39.783
but I'll use it now.

27:42.160 --> 27:44.705
You said it's okay
to keep some secrets to yourself.

27:44.788 --> 27:46.874
You tell me a secret too next time.

27:46.957 --> 27:48.876
We can keep big secrets to ourselves.

27:48.959 --> 27:50.878
Just a small one.

27:50.961 --> 27:54.423
I'll tell you everything
about the present…

27:55.048 --> 27:57.301
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

27:57.384 --> 27:58.719
but I'll use that card…

28:00.637 --> 28:01.889
for my past.

28:03.390 --> 28:04.391
Sorry.

28:06.852 --> 28:07.853
Ah…

28:08.770 --> 28:09.771
Oh, no.

28:09.855 --> 28:11.940
I guess I was being really rude.

28:12.566 --> 28:15.611
[stutters] Right, we agreed
to do a three-month trial,

28:15.694 --> 28:17.487
but I was prying too much.

28:18.530 --> 28:21.241
[stutters] I was being selfish.
I'm so sorry.

28:27.331 --> 28:28.332
[♪ music ends]

28:31.084 --> 28:32.085
[men chuckling]

28:32.169 --> 28:33.295
[talking indistinctly]

28:33.378 --> 28:35.881
This looks so delicious.

28:36.548 --> 28:37.674
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

28:39.718 --> 28:41.762
-[in English] Thank you.
-Yeah, no problem.

28:41.845 --> 28:45.140
[in Korean] The staff prepared this since
the costume team is leaving tomorrow.

28:45.223 --> 28:47.434
-Thank you.
-That's so nice.

28:47.517 --> 28:48.727
I'm so touched.

28:48.810 --> 28:50.854
Do we seriously have to leave this behind

28:50.938 --> 28:52.898
-and return to Seoul?
-[sighs]

28:52.981 --> 28:55.192
[sighs] I can't leave!

28:55.275 --> 28:57.986
Since this is our last night,

28:58.070 --> 28:59.988
let us all have a drink.

29:00.072 --> 29:02.491
[indistinct chatter]

29:02.574 --> 29:04.034
Everyone… [in English] Cheers!

29:04.117 --> 29:07.079
[group] Cheers! [exclaiming]

29:07.162 --> 29:09.539
[in Korean] ♪ Altogether
Game start ♪

29:09.623 --> 29:10.916
-Numbers game! One!
-Two!

29:10.999 --> 29:12.000
Three!

29:12.084 --> 29:13.335
-[Sol cheers]
-[guest laughs]

29:13.418 --> 29:15.629
-[all in English] Drink!
-[exclaims]

29:15.712 --> 29:16.838
[in Korean] ♪ Drink up ♪

29:16.922 --> 29:18.465
It's my first time seeing her drink.

29:18.548 --> 29:20.550
Wait, stop. I have to film this.

29:20.634 --> 29:22.427
-[Sol] Can you drink like a beer model?
-[exclaims]

29:22.511 --> 29:24.179
No…

29:24.262 --> 29:26.181
-[Sol cheers, applauds]
-Why are you so pretty?

29:27.975 --> 29:28.976
[sighs]

29:29.059 --> 29:31.269
♪ Altogether
Game start ♪

29:31.353 --> 29:32.479
♪ Three, six, nine ♪

29:32.562 --> 29:33.689
[all] ♪ Three, six, nine ♪

29:33.772 --> 29:36.692
[game continues indistinctly]

29:40.278 --> 29:42.739
Why are you suddenly so serious?
It doesn't suit you.

29:43.240 --> 29:44.866
[inhales deeply] Ben.

29:45.367 --> 29:46.743
Hiding something

29:47.577 --> 29:49.287
and not telling the truth

29:50.622 --> 29:52.582
is the same as lying, right?

29:53.166 --> 29:54.167
That's so random.

29:55.335 --> 29:56.420
Hide what, though?

29:56.503 --> 30:01.341
You mean like how Aladdin
hid the fact that he was a petty thief?

30:01.425 --> 30:02.426
[chuckles softly]

30:03.260 --> 30:04.845
I guess it's similar.

30:06.388 --> 30:07.639
It's just…

30:07.723 --> 30:10.559
The other person is being honest with me,

30:12.227 --> 30:13.770
but if I keep…

30:15.397 --> 30:16.648
hiding things

30:17.482 --> 30:19.359
and never being honest,

30:20.485 --> 30:22.279
what will happen in the end?

30:24.823 --> 30:25.824
Ah.

30:27.242 --> 30:28.285
Do you remember?

30:28.994 --> 30:32.039
[in English] What the genie says
to Aladdin when he says

30:33.123 --> 30:35.042
he wants to keep pretending
to be a prince?

30:36.209 --> 30:37.210
Mmm.

30:38.587 --> 30:42.758
[in Korean] The more you gain
with deception,

30:45.093 --> 30:48.346
the less you can truly gain.

30:48.764 --> 30:49.848
That's right.

30:51.016 --> 30:53.435
It may seem like
you're gaining something now,

30:53.518 --> 30:56.354
but you'll probably end up
paying the price for it.

30:57.814 --> 30:59.024
Paying the price…

30:59.107 --> 31:01.151
[waves crashing]

31:02.736 --> 31:05.155
[indistinct chatter]

31:21.505 --> 31:22.964
What are you doing here alone?

31:23.882 --> 31:24.883
[chuckles softly]

31:25.509 --> 31:27.469
I'm trying to sober up
so I can drink more.

31:28.136 --> 31:29.846
It's been a while since I drank.

31:30.555 --> 31:31.973
You're a heavy drinker.

31:32.599 --> 31:34.017
How's your foot?

31:34.601 --> 31:36.853
You hurt yourself
because of Grandma's scarf.

31:37.771 --> 31:38.814
I'm okay.

31:39.481 --> 31:40.482
[Haran grunts]

31:43.026 --> 31:44.027
[Chan grunts]

31:45.153 --> 31:46.154
Look, aren't they pretty?

31:48.490 --> 31:50.325
-[chuckles]
-[sighs]

31:50.826 --> 31:54.121
Maybe it's because I lost
the pen I used for seven years,

31:54.204 --> 31:56.748
but I couldn't sketch anything
during the two days here.

31:57.958 --> 32:00.502
Maybe it's because
I couldn't stop thinking about it.

32:00.585 --> 32:02.420
I've been so distracted lately.

32:03.839 --> 32:09.052
Until now, I thought that pen was special
because of the person who gifted it to me.

32:10.595 --> 32:12.430
But I'm not so sure now.

32:12.973 --> 32:15.559
Maybe I just feel strange

32:15.642 --> 32:18.562
because I lost something
my hand had gotten used to

32:18.645 --> 32:21.022
after all those years.

32:23.692 --> 32:26.611
The person who gave me that pen died.

32:28.363 --> 32:30.949
I guess that's why
I was so attached to it.

32:31.992 --> 32:33.827
Not long ago,

32:33.910 --> 32:37.914
I would have done anything I could
to avoid coming here.

32:37.998 --> 32:39.499
But this time,

32:40.000 --> 32:43.003
I had quite a lot of fun.

32:43.545 --> 32:44.921
Like I was on a spring picnic.

32:45.005 --> 32:46.798
[♪ pleasant music playing]

32:46.882 --> 32:48.758
I guess we have grown quite close,

32:49.426 --> 32:52.721
seeing how I'm telling you
things I'm not okay with.

32:53.889 --> 32:57.809
You know we're not real friends
if we're always pretending to be okay.

33:02.522 --> 33:05.192
Thank you for asking to be friends

33:06.651 --> 33:08.153
and for knocking on my door.

33:09.112 --> 33:10.614
You made me stop hiding,

33:11.656 --> 33:15.869
and you made me
able to tell you sad things, too.

33:17.996 --> 33:20.624
Stop thanking me. I didn't do anything.

33:20.707 --> 33:22.125
Thank you.

33:22.209 --> 33:24.878
I just feel like
pouring my heart out today.

33:26.463 --> 33:28.173
I really am grateful.

33:36.473 --> 33:39.226
[sighs] Can I borrow that for a moment?

33:40.560 --> 33:41.853
-This?
-Yes.

33:50.278 --> 33:51.279
Odd or even?

33:51.738 --> 33:53.240
That's so random.

33:53.323 --> 33:55.408
Is there a prize if I guess right?

33:57.118 --> 33:58.119
If you guess right,

34:00.163 --> 34:02.165
I'll tell you everything.

34:03.124 --> 34:04.292
I feel like

34:05.752 --> 34:07.712
telling you everything today, too.

34:08.922 --> 34:11.258
-Tell me what?
-I think I should stop

34:11.341 --> 34:12.592
hiding things about myself.

34:13.885 --> 34:14.970
Oh…

34:15.053 --> 34:17.722
If it's because of what I said,
you don't have to--

34:17.806 --> 34:18.974
Odd or even?

34:19.057 --> 34:20.517
[♪ pleasant music continuing]

34:33.363 --> 34:34.364
Odd.

34:45.667 --> 34:46.793
Odd.

34:46.876 --> 34:47.877
[♪ music fades]

34:51.923 --> 34:52.924
[sighs contentedly]

34:53.008 --> 34:54.801
[cell phone pinging]

34:54.884 --> 34:57.012
[grumbles] Who keeps messaging?

34:57.095 --> 34:58.513
It's me.

34:59.097 --> 35:01.016
I'm uploading our photos
to our group chat.

35:01.099 --> 35:02.517
-[Raemee chuckles]
-[Sol] Oh…

35:03.727 --> 35:04.936
[cell phone vibrates]

35:05.937 --> 35:08.565
-[Sol] Mmm.
-Hi, Hayeong. Did you see…

35:10.984 --> 35:11.985
[in English] What?

35:13.111 --> 35:14.613
[in Korean] I'm not sure…

35:16.740 --> 35:18.825
if I have the right to tell you

35:20.577 --> 35:21.911
about myself.

35:23.121 --> 35:24.331
To be honest…

35:28.543 --> 35:29.544
I'm scared.

35:30.879 --> 35:34.174
You asked me what happened in America.

35:35.842 --> 35:36.968
I…

35:39.888 --> 35:41.014
was actually…

35:45.560 --> 35:47.604
in Boston, attending…

35:48.855 --> 35:49.856
[exclaims]

35:51.358 --> 35:52.817
[Hayeong] Haran's a total lightweight.

35:52.901 --> 35:54.277
She can't drink a single drop.

35:54.361 --> 35:55.737
Don't let her drink anything.

35:55.820 --> 35:58.531
-[Raemee in English] Stop!
-[in Korean] She can't drink at all!

35:58.615 --> 36:00.533
-Wait!
-Ms. Song!

36:01.159 --> 36:03.161
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

36:17.884 --> 36:18.885
[sighs softly]

36:21.096 --> 36:23.098
[bells chiming in distance]

36:27.977 --> 36:28.978
[♪ music fades]

36:36.027 --> 36:38.029
[chiming continues]

36:39.739 --> 36:41.991
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

36:46.621 --> 36:48.289
[Hyeokchan] Hey. Sorry, Haran.

36:48.998 --> 36:50.166
That song?

36:50.250 --> 36:52.210
Okay, I'll listen to it.

36:52.293 --> 36:54.421
Can you message her back?

36:54.504 --> 36:55.922
Sorry. Do me a solid.

36:56.005 --> 36:58.049
Anything that a woman
in her twenties can use.

36:58.133 --> 37:01.386
I have to go to the hospital
because of my hand. [echoing]

37:09.728 --> 37:11.479
-[shatters]
-[Hyeokchan groans, inhales sharply]

37:14.691 --> 37:16.401
[Hyeokchan groans, inhales sharply]

37:16.484 --> 37:18.027
[♪ music continues]

37:21.614 --> 37:23.700
-[patient exclaims]
-[metallic clink echoing]

37:25.535 --> 37:26.661
[in English] Sorry.

37:26.745 --> 37:29.914
-[in Korean] Thanks, Chan.
-Who's that? Your friend?

37:29.998 --> 37:31.624
[Hyeokchan] No, just my roommate.

37:34.002 --> 37:36.379
Sorry, Ran. My professor's calling.

37:36.463 --> 37:37.714
I'll call you back later.

37:39.257 --> 37:40.300
Sujin. You're here?

37:40.800 --> 37:41.801
I'll head out now.

37:44.387 --> 37:45.430
I'll be away for a few weeks.

37:45.513 --> 37:48.308
I'm traveling around the East Coast
during vacation.

37:49.100 --> 37:52.896
If our professor asks for me,
say I'm taking a break because of my hand.

37:56.232 --> 37:58.860
[clinking]

38:04.115 --> 38:05.909
[clinking echoes]

38:05.992 --> 38:06.993
[♪ music fades]

38:08.703 --> 38:10.622
[metallic clink echoes]

38:10.705 --> 38:11.790
[thud echoes]

38:11.873 --> 38:13.625
[high-pitched ringing]

38:13.750 --> 38:15.752
[♪ dramatic music playing]

38:18.755 --> 38:22.258
[Haran] Getting close to someone
is really difficult…

38:22.342 --> 38:24.177
No, it's scary for me.

38:25.053 --> 38:28.932
[Haran vocalizing "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" by J.S. Bach on phone]

38:33.144 --> 38:36.523
[♪ J.S. Bach "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" plays on earphones]

38:36.606 --> 38:38.817
[Haran] It's all thanks to this pen.

38:38.900 --> 38:40.944
It's really valuable to me,
so I have to find it.

38:41.027 --> 38:42.445
[♪ dramatic music continues]

38:42.529 --> 38:44.364
Chan, I saw a vapor trail earlier.

38:44.447 --> 38:47.283
But that made me want
to get on a plane to go see you.

38:48.910 --> 38:51.120
Whether you're a guy or not,
I don't want to get close.

38:57.293 --> 39:00.922
-[♪ music climaxes, fades]
-[gasping]

39:01.005 --> 39:03.007
[♪ dramatic music continues]

39:14.018 --> 39:16.312
[breathing shakily]

39:22.652 --> 39:24.654
[sobbing echoes]

39:34.664 --> 39:35.665
[♪ music fades]

39:36.332 --> 39:37.333
[gasps]

39:38.376 --> 39:40.086
[exclaims softly, gasps]

39:41.880 --> 39:44.007
It's morning?

39:45.341 --> 39:46.342
[gasps]

39:54.183 --> 39:56.019
-[floor creaks]
-[door slides shut]

39:56.603 --> 39:58.897
Hey. You spoke as if you were
a heavy drinker,

39:58.980 --> 40:03.443
but you passed out right away. [chuckles]

40:04.360 --> 40:08.823
I don't usually pass out
after drinking like that,

40:08.907 --> 40:11.451
but the alcohol tasted really good.

40:11.534 --> 40:15.288
Maybe it was because the weather
was so nice. [chuckles awkwardly]

40:19.292 --> 40:20.376
Hey, Sujin.

40:20.460 --> 40:21.920
[metallic clink echoes]

40:24.172 --> 40:26.299
It's okay to be a lightweight.

40:26.382 --> 40:28.051
Why are you looking at me with pity?

40:28.134 --> 40:30.386
No, I'm not looking at you that way.

40:30.470 --> 40:33.681
You are. You just looked at me
like I was a lost puppy.

40:37.185 --> 40:38.186
[Chan] Hmm.

40:39.729 --> 40:40.730
[inhales sharply]

40:42.023 --> 40:44.859
It's pitiful that
you're waiting for your old owner.

40:44.943 --> 40:47.779
I should be good to you
so you won't remember them.

40:49.322 --> 40:50.990
Is that how I looked at you?

40:52.200 --> 40:53.660
No need to say it like that…

40:54.285 --> 40:56.245
Let's go. Oh.

40:56.329 --> 40:58.498
-Bring your jacket.
-Where are we going?

40:59.082 --> 41:00.792
A hangover cure walk?

41:00.875 --> 41:03.836
If walking cured hangovers,
hangover soup places would close down.

41:05.380 --> 41:08.883
But when exactly did I pass out?

41:09.968 --> 41:11.135
Don't you remember?

41:12.512 --> 41:13.680
This.

41:17.308 --> 41:19.018
Right. Odd or even.

41:19.602 --> 41:23.189
[groans] I should have said odd.
Why did I guess even?

41:24.023 --> 41:26.567
-You didn't…
-Let's just say I did.

41:27.819 --> 41:30.655
There's no need to know everything.

41:30.738 --> 41:31.739
Still…

41:31.823 --> 41:34.534
You used your card
so you wouldn't have to tell me.

41:34.617 --> 41:36.452
It must have been something bad.

41:37.120 --> 41:39.330
I don't want to force you
to talk about it.

41:40.331 --> 41:43.751
There's no need to dig into your scars
to learn more about you.

41:47.797 --> 41:49.924
And even if I don't know about it,

41:50.842 --> 41:52.844
we're already quite close, right?

41:58.850 --> 42:01.185
[inhales sharply] Oh, right.

42:01.269 --> 42:02.520
Here.

42:02.603 --> 42:03.730
Honey water.

42:03.813 --> 42:05.857
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

42:05.940 --> 42:09.360
Hangover medicine, hangover drink,

42:09.444 --> 42:12.321
-roasted eggs, and…
-[Haran gasps]

42:12.989 --> 42:14.866
They must have been really kind to you.

42:15.408 --> 42:16.409
Who?

42:16.492 --> 42:19.579
The person who showed you
a way to keep going.

42:20.496 --> 42:21.998
The one who kept reaching out.

42:23.124 --> 42:26.044
I just wondered
if you're so sweet to other people

42:26.127 --> 42:28.588
because you learned it from them.

42:31.591 --> 42:34.302
[inhales sharply, sighs]

42:34.385 --> 42:36.345
How should I say it…

42:36.971 --> 42:38.222
I'm no match.

42:39.140 --> 42:41.350
This is nothing
compared to what I received.

42:41.434 --> 42:43.644
I received something so incredible

42:44.562 --> 42:46.022
that I could never repay her.

42:48.191 --> 42:49.484
Was it your girlfriend?

42:49.567 --> 42:52.570
No, of course not. I wouldn't dare.

42:53.946 --> 42:56.157
It wasn't like that. Mmm…

42:56.991 --> 42:57.992
She was just…

42:59.535 --> 43:02.538
someone who broadened my world.

43:03.206 --> 43:05.124
Broadened your world?

43:05.208 --> 43:06.209
Yes.

43:07.794 --> 43:09.670
She let me experience things

43:11.005 --> 43:12.757
that I couldn't see or feel before.

43:14.133 --> 43:18.096
My world used to be
black and white, but she…

43:20.098 --> 43:21.974
filled it with vibrant colors.

43:26.354 --> 43:28.147
[inhales sharply] Right. High five!

43:28.773 --> 43:30.983
I have a habit of doing high fives
when I'm grateful.

43:31.567 --> 43:33.402
You're grateful? All of a sudden?

43:34.529 --> 43:35.738
I found the answer.

43:36.864 --> 43:39.742
My choice was filled with question marks,

43:40.284 --> 43:44.163
but you just changed them
to exclamation marks.

43:45.706 --> 43:46.707
Your choice?

43:46.791 --> 43:48.417
I chose never to do anything

43:48.501 --> 43:52.380
that might get in the way
of her happiness.

43:53.297 --> 43:55.716
Thanks to you, I just realized

43:56.342 --> 43:59.887
that not digging up old wounds
is also a way…

44:01.347 --> 44:03.724
of protecting their happiness.

44:04.892 --> 44:06.435
That's why I'm asking

44:07.186 --> 44:08.187
for a high five.

44:09.063 --> 44:12.024
Well, I have no idea
what you're talking about,

44:12.108 --> 44:14.152
but since you say I helped…

44:14.902 --> 44:15.903
[chuckles softly]

44:23.911 --> 44:24.912
[♪ music ends]

44:24.996 --> 44:26.914
[Hayeong retches] Two green onions…

44:29.292 --> 44:31.502
[retches] Three green onions…

44:33.379 --> 44:35.047
Isn't that for your hangover?

44:35.131 --> 44:37.508
Why are you making art
instead of eating it?

44:37.592 --> 44:41.345
I may be friendly with everyone,
but not green onions…

44:42.430 --> 44:44.724
What? Hang on.

44:45.641 --> 44:46.642
Mmm.

44:47.852 --> 44:50.021
He picked out the green onions for me.

44:50.104 --> 44:52.273
How did he know I don't eat green onions?

44:52.899 --> 44:55.818
Green onions… What does that mean?

44:56.694 --> 44:58.029
Did he flirt with green onions?

44:58.112 --> 44:59.739
I'm heading out now.

44:59.822 --> 45:01.032
Right, the tonics.

45:01.115 --> 45:05.203
I should take a tonic
that Mr. Yeon gave me.

45:05.286 --> 45:06.579
-Huh?
-[Nana] Oh.

45:06.662 --> 45:09.999
I should take the vitamins
that Mr. Yeon got me.

45:10.082 --> 45:11.876
-What?
-He seemed a bit reserved,

45:11.959 --> 45:13.377
but he takes care of our whole family.

45:13.461 --> 45:15.254
He's so thoughtful.

45:15.338 --> 45:17.632
-I'll get going now.
-See you.

45:17.715 --> 45:19.091
Okay.

45:20.301 --> 45:21.302
[stutters] Grandma.

45:22.094 --> 45:26.641
Did Mr. Yeon always
take care of everyone like this?

45:26.724 --> 45:28.476
What's the point of having you three?

45:28.559 --> 45:30.561
Mr. Yeon's the only one
who takes care of me.

45:33.022 --> 45:34.482
Geez.

45:35.274 --> 45:37.443
I was overreacting for no reason.

45:40.696 --> 45:41.697
Gosh, that's hot.

45:41.781 --> 45:44.617
-Great work.
-Great work, everyone.

45:44.700 --> 45:46.077
-Thank you.
-[Sol] Great work.

45:46.160 --> 45:47.703
[Ben] Thank you for everything.

45:49.038 --> 45:50.581
I'll see you in Seoul.

45:50.665 --> 45:52.333
Okay. I'll see you in 10 days.

45:52.875 --> 45:54.669
Oh. That's a day for pizza.

45:54.752 --> 45:56.671
How about pizza that day?

45:58.172 --> 46:00.174
-Is it a full moon? [chuckles softly]
-Mmm.

46:00.258 --> 46:01.676
Sure, pizza sounds good.

46:01.759 --> 46:03.678
And here.

46:04.804 --> 46:06.514
For the hangover stuff you gave me.

46:06.597 --> 46:08.182
HANG IN THERE!

46:08.641 --> 46:10.643
[chuckles softly] I also have…

46:11.894 --> 46:12.895
this.

46:13.604 --> 46:14.605
Hmm?

46:15.231 --> 46:16.232
Homework.

46:17.066 --> 46:18.067
[Haran] A film camera?

46:18.150 --> 46:19.610
What kind of homework?

46:19.694 --> 46:21.404
Well…

46:22.530 --> 46:24.532
Ms. Song, hurry.

46:24.615 --> 46:25.700
Come on.

46:26.742 --> 46:28.369
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

46:28.953 --> 46:30.454
Hurry!

46:32.623 --> 46:34.792
It would be a huge waste not to see that.

46:37.837 --> 46:40.756
-[Haran] Wow, it's beautiful.
-[camera clicks]

46:40.840 --> 46:42.925
It's called an iridescent cloud.

46:43.884 --> 46:45.011
An iridescent cloud?

46:45.094 --> 46:47.096
[Chan] We also call them
mother-of-pearl clouds.

46:47.179 --> 46:50.391
Because of the diffraction of sunlight,
the cloud particles…

46:50.474 --> 46:52.101
Forget it.

46:52.685 --> 46:54.186
It's a good omen.

46:54.270 --> 46:56.939
They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

46:58.024 --> 46:59.442
That's childish.

47:00.735 --> 47:02.236
Do people say it's lucky?

47:04.030 --> 47:05.281
[chuckles]

47:05.364 --> 47:07.241
-[camera clicks]
-Wait, it's blurry.

47:08.826 --> 47:09.827
[inhales deeply]

47:10.536 --> 47:14.957
You should look for iridescent clouds
in the sky, too,

47:15.041 --> 47:16.709
instead of just vapor trails.

47:18.502 --> 47:19.503
[♪ music fades]

47:19.587 --> 47:24.342
Vapor trails are just traces
of something that already passed by.

47:25.134 --> 47:28.721
But iridescent clouds
make you excited for the future.

47:28.804 --> 47:29.805
[♪ music continues]

47:29.889 --> 47:31.140
The past…

47:32.892 --> 47:36.520
may not be as beautiful as you remember.

47:37.063 --> 47:39.774
They get blurred,
overwritten, and distorted.

47:40.941 --> 47:44.445
Or they may have been romanticized
because some things…

47:45.446 --> 47:46.739
were hidden.

47:48.866 --> 47:50.785
Why are you suddenly saying that?

47:50.868 --> 47:51.869
I was just…

47:52.870 --> 47:55.956
worried that you'd miss
an iridescent cloud

47:56.040 --> 47:57.333
while staring at a vapor trail.

47:58.793 --> 48:01.796
I have a habit of feeling upset
if I miss something exciting

48:01.879 --> 48:04.382
while thinking about the past.
[chuckles softly]

48:05.257 --> 48:06.258
[♪ music fades]

48:06.384 --> 48:08.094
[Raemee] All right, everybody. Come here!

48:08.177 --> 48:10.179
-Ending a trip…
-With a group photo…

48:10.262 --> 48:12.765
[group] ...is a must!

48:12.848 --> 48:14.016
Let's go.

48:14.100 --> 48:16.519
-[♪ pleasant music playing]
-[lively chatter]

48:16.602 --> 48:20.606
[indistinct chatter]

48:20.689 --> 48:22.733
[Sol] All right. Here goes.

48:22.817 --> 48:24.026
[Raemee] Hurry.

48:24.110 --> 48:26.237
Okay, everyone. What's one plus one?

48:26.320 --> 48:29.198
-[all] Two!
-[in English] Two!

48:31.784 --> 48:33.994
[♪ uplifting song playing]

48:51.303 --> 48:52.888
[Haran] But what sort of homework is this?

48:52.972 --> 48:54.515
Take one photo each day

48:54.598 --> 48:56.559
and show them to me
when I return to Seoul.

48:56.642 --> 48:58.686
Isn't it crazy, though?

48:58.769 --> 49:01.397
How did they know I'm leaving in 10 days

49:01.480 --> 49:04.024
and sell a 10-shot camera?
[chuckles softly]

49:04.108 --> 49:06.068
What should I take photos of?

49:06.152 --> 49:09.071
Something fun, delicious, or pretty.

49:09.155 --> 49:12.825
Just anything
that made you feel good that day.

49:25.337 --> 49:27.089
[Haran] Hang in there!

49:33.179 --> 49:34.221
[sighs contentedly]

49:41.103 --> 49:42.104
[♪ song fades]

49:43.022 --> 49:45.858
-I'd like some coffee.
-It's on me, so help yourselves!

49:45.941 --> 49:48.152
-[Sol] This is so good!
-I got us some coffee.

49:48.235 --> 49:49.403
[Seunggyu] What's with the coffee?

49:49.487 --> 49:52.656
I heard Je Raemee was bringing
Gyeongju bread today.

49:52.740 --> 49:54.492
I thought it would go well with coffee.

49:54.575 --> 49:55.701
Can I have one?

49:56.785 --> 49:58.120
Wasn't Gyeongju amazing?

49:58.204 --> 50:02.666
There were so many things to see and eat,
and the beach was so beautiful…

50:04.251 --> 50:05.544
What is it?

50:05.628 --> 50:09.298
We've never seen you talk for so long
about something other than work.

50:09.381 --> 50:11.383
It's the first time since I joined.

50:13.052 --> 50:14.678
[♪ whimsical music playing]

50:14.762 --> 50:16.639
Let's start working, then.

50:21.769 --> 50:23.604
[scoffs] She's suddenly
acting so friendly.

50:24.396 --> 50:27.942
Well, she's not tinting her windows
or brooding like before.

50:28.025 --> 50:31.862
I guess she's a tiny bit… better
than before.

50:31.946 --> 50:32.947
[elevator dings]

50:34.240 --> 50:36.575
-Hello.
-[buttons beep]

50:37.201 --> 50:40.955
[inhales sharply, grunts]

50:41.038 --> 50:42.289
[yawns]

50:43.749 --> 50:46.460
Wow. You and sweet and sour candy?

50:47.086 --> 50:48.462
That really doesn't suit you.

50:48.546 --> 50:51.507
Ah. I guess you're giving it to someone.

50:52.341 --> 50:53.342
Pardon?

50:53.926 --> 50:55.886
Would you like one?

50:56.470 --> 50:57.638
Sure.

50:58.138 --> 50:59.974
-[elevator dings]
-I'll try one, then.

51:01.350 --> 51:02.434
Thank you.

51:04.520 --> 51:05.604
[hums delightedly]

51:06.564 --> 51:07.982
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

51:18.242 --> 51:19.243
Hello.

51:19.326 --> 51:22.037
I'm Yeon Taeseok
from Seoul Commercial High School.

51:22.121 --> 51:24.999
[exclaims] Mr. Yeon Taeseok.

51:25.082 --> 51:27.167
Even your name sounds proper.

51:28.127 --> 51:30.212
But you said hello to the wrong person.

51:30.713 --> 51:33.090
Oh… Sorry.

51:33.173 --> 51:35.801
[stutters] No need to apologize.

51:36.302 --> 51:39.680
Wow. You're sweating a lot.

51:40.806 --> 51:42.474
[chuckles] Ah.

51:44.018 --> 51:45.436
Would you like one?

51:45.519 --> 51:46.604
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

51:46.687 --> 51:49.106
The sour taste will snap you awake,

51:49.189 --> 51:51.150
and the sweet taste will help you relax.

51:52.026 --> 51:54.778
Eat that to relax your nerves.

51:54.862 --> 51:55.988
Thank you.

51:56.071 --> 51:57.072
And…

51:57.698 --> 51:59.617
There's a piece of tissue here.

52:00.326 --> 52:03.120
[chuckles softly] Then good luck.

52:03.203 --> 52:05.289
-You can do it.
-Right.

52:06.957 --> 52:08.125
[sighs]

52:08.208 --> 52:11.086
I tried to get some pocket money
from Grandma but got a noogie.

52:18.218 --> 52:19.303
[exhales]

52:19.928 --> 52:23.098
Mr. Yeon Taeseok,
Ms. Kim will see you now.

52:23.182 --> 52:24.183
Okay.

52:33.275 --> 52:34.360
[softly] Thank you.

52:39.239 --> 52:40.240
[♪ music fades]

52:40.324 --> 52:41.742
[indistinct chatter]

52:43.786 --> 52:44.828
I'll be right back.

52:45.329 --> 52:46.538
Hadam!

52:51.085 --> 52:53.128
Are you going to your math academy?

52:53.796 --> 52:55.631
What is it?

52:55.714 --> 52:57.591
You look worried about something.

52:58.967 --> 53:01.887
What is it?
Tell your boyfriend everything.

53:03.681 --> 53:04.973
Yougyum.

53:07.226 --> 53:10.354
Did you go to a jewelry shop
a few days ago…

53:10.437 --> 53:11.897
-[players exclaim teasingly]
-Hey, Yougyum!

53:11.980 --> 53:15.234
Enough with the PDA and get back here.
We have to practice.

53:15.901 --> 53:18.404
Go on. We'll talk later.

53:18.487 --> 53:20.614
I'll call you later.

53:20.698 --> 53:22.616
[♪ amusing music playing]

53:25.285 --> 53:28.497
If anything is bothering you, tell me.
I'll take care of everything…

53:28.580 --> 53:31.208
I mean, everything besides studying.

53:31.291 --> 53:33.836
[giggles] All right.

53:34.920 --> 53:36.922
Hang in there! [giggles]

53:38.757 --> 53:41.176
[scoffs] Park Yeseul…

53:41.260 --> 53:44.054
Why did she have to bring up
Han Sora? [chuckles softly]

53:45.139 --> 53:47.224
[cell phone vibrating]

53:47.307 --> 53:48.892
CHA YOUGYUM

53:51.061 --> 53:53.355
SORA

53:53.439 --> 53:54.440
-[vibrating]
-[♪ music ends]

53:55.482 --> 53:56.525
Yes, Ms. Kim.

53:58.152 --> 53:59.528
The revised sketch?

54:00.195 --> 54:02.197
No. I'll hand it in by today.

54:03.657 --> 54:04.742
Okay.

54:06.326 --> 54:07.327
[line disconnects]

54:08.203 --> 54:11.457
[groans] I really need an idea. Please…

54:11.540 --> 54:13.542
-[whines]
-[cell phone buzzes]

54:15.377 --> 54:16.587
[sighs exasperatedly]

54:17.963 --> 54:20.090
[Chan] I'm sending you a photo
since you said yours was blurry.

54:25.512 --> 54:26.805
[chuckles softly]

54:27.514 --> 54:28.515
[knock on door]

54:28.599 --> 54:30.726
Ms. Song, the material check…

54:31.393 --> 54:34.396
[gasps loudly] What happened to your hair?

54:35.147 --> 54:38.317
Whoa. What's that? The colors are amazing.

54:38.400 --> 54:42.196
I saw it for the first time in Gyeongju.
It's called an iridescent cloud.

54:42.279 --> 54:43.530
[Sol] It's a cloud?

54:43.614 --> 54:45.199
Wow. It looks like a rainbow.

54:45.282 --> 54:47.242
They call it a rainbow cloud, too.

54:47.868 --> 54:49.661
It's also called a mother-of-pearl cloud…

54:51.079 --> 54:52.706
because of the color…

54:52.789 --> 54:54.124
[♪ pleasant music playing]

54:57.920 --> 55:01.590
-Oh. Can you get my rolling cart?
-What?

55:02.633 --> 55:03.675
Right.

55:15.395 --> 55:16.396
[sniffs]

55:33.539 --> 55:35.290
Here's the revised outfit design.

55:35.874 --> 55:37.501
Sorry, I'm late.

55:45.759 --> 55:47.803
-It wasn't just a simple revision.
-[♪ music ends]

55:47.886 --> 55:52.015
The color was important,
so I made a colored illustration.

55:52.099 --> 55:54.685
That's a color palette
I haven't seen before.

55:54.768 --> 55:59.064
I applied mother-of-pearl colors
on the basic silhouette.

55:59.147 --> 56:01.817
Mother-of-pearl…

56:01.900 --> 56:03.819
-As in shiny seashells?
-Yes.

56:03.902 --> 56:08.615
I thought it could be a great material
to highlight a Korean aesthetic.

56:08.699 --> 56:12.703
For now, I just expressed
the general vibe with gloss pens,

56:12.786 --> 56:15.497
but if we can capture
the texture of mother-of-pearl

56:15.581 --> 56:17.958
so it has a mysterious glow
whenever she moves,

56:18.041 --> 56:20.919
I think that would add some fun
to the animation as well.

56:21.003 --> 56:22.254
Well…

56:22.337 --> 56:23.505
Not bad.

56:24.047 --> 56:26.008
Mother-of-pearl is normally used
for decorations.

56:26.592 --> 56:28.552
How did you come up with the idea
of using its colors?

56:28.635 --> 56:29.636
Oh…

56:30.512 --> 56:33.557
This is an iridescent cloud
I saw in Gyeongju.

56:33.640 --> 56:35.976
This photo became a great inspiration.

56:36.059 --> 56:38.604
I heard it's also called
a mother-of-pearl cloud

56:38.687 --> 56:39.730
because of its colors.

56:39.813 --> 56:41.064
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

56:41.148 --> 56:42.316
[Nana] Mmm.

56:42.399 --> 56:47.487
It will go well with Raemee's idea
of emphasizing the collar and front panel.

56:50.032 --> 56:51.325
So that trip wasn't for nothing.

56:52.993 --> 56:54.202
You can go.

56:55.412 --> 56:56.580
Okay.

57:01.543 --> 57:02.544
[sighs]

57:04.796 --> 57:06.381
She won't need me anymore.

57:09.217 --> 57:10.469
-[cell phone buzzes]
-Hmm?

57:11.428 --> 57:13.013
[Haran] My sketch finally got accepted.

57:18.894 --> 57:20.896
Huh? Wait.

57:20.979 --> 57:23.106
Was this inspired
by that iridescent cloud?

57:23.190 --> 57:26.360
[Haran] That's right. You said it's also
called a mother-of-pearl cloud.

57:27.027 --> 57:29.404
It's all thanks to you.
I'll treat you to 10 pizzas.

57:32.991 --> 57:34.576
[inhales sharply] Let's see…

57:46.713 --> 57:48.715
Mmm… [sighs]

57:50.175 --> 57:52.844
[Chan] They say you have good luck
if you see an iridescent cloud.

57:53.553 --> 57:55.639
-He was right.
-[♪ music fades]

57:55.722 --> 57:58.850
[sighs in relief] It worked out
thanks to him. [chuckles softly]

58:00.477 --> 58:01.853
The cloud you saw in Gyeongju?

58:02.771 --> 58:06.733
[inhales deeply] Why do I feel like
I know who you saw it with?

58:06.817 --> 58:07.818
What?

58:07.901 --> 58:12.739
The Haran before wasn't my style,
so she was about 0.5 points,

58:12.823 --> 58:15.575
but the new Song Haran
after our Gyeongju trip… Tsk.

58:16.076 --> 58:17.452
Right, I'll give you three points.

58:18.078 --> 58:19.746
Fine. I'll give you 3.5.

58:20.664 --> 58:22.582
-Excuse me?
-Don't get too excited.

58:22.666 --> 58:24.000
My points…

58:24.793 --> 58:26.712
are out of 10.

58:26.795 --> 58:28.505
[♪ amusing music plays]

58:33.844 --> 58:35.220
All right.

58:43.603 --> 58:46.690
[inhales sharply]
Didn't I tell you to stop coming?

58:53.155 --> 58:54.364
[Yougyum] It's grated yam.

58:54.448 --> 58:56.533
I did some research,
and they said it helps.

58:57.033 --> 58:59.578
I'm already taking good care of myself.

58:59.661 --> 59:02.164
Just focus on baseball.

59:02.247 --> 59:05.000
I'm practicing really hard too, you know.

59:06.626 --> 59:09.588
But what about
that examination you mentioned last time?

59:09.671 --> 59:10.672
It's next week.

59:11.548 --> 59:14.050
Are you getting along well with Hadam?

59:14.134 --> 59:16.386
Why aren't you talking
about marriage anymore?

59:16.470 --> 59:20.390
I decided to support her quietly
until the CSAT so I wouldn't distract her.

59:20.974 --> 59:23.101
Have you been wearing
that necklace I gave you?

59:23.185 --> 59:25.187
If it's not the right length, I can…

59:25.270 --> 59:26.563
GUARDIAN

59:27.397 --> 59:29.691
You're just a student.
Where did you get the money?

59:29.775 --> 59:32.360
I'm a future Major Leaguer, you know.

59:32.444 --> 59:35.739
Gosh. I should get
an autograph in advance.

59:35.822 --> 59:36.948
[both chuckle]

59:38.492 --> 59:41.953
Huh? Did you hit your leg somewhere?

59:42.537 --> 59:44.956
It's fine. I just fell.

59:45.707 --> 59:47.626
My legs suddenly wouldn't listen.

59:52.088 --> 59:55.801
You have to make sure
Hadam doesn't find out until the CSAT.

59:57.886 --> 01:00:01.515
Okay. I'll take good care of her.

01:00:04.059 --> 01:00:05.060
[chuckles softly]

01:00:06.853 --> 01:00:08.480
[cell phone vibrating]

01:00:13.777 --> 01:00:16.112
-Hello?
-Are you free next next Friday at 7 p.m.?

01:00:16.196 --> 01:00:18.073
Next next Friday?

01:00:19.199 --> 01:00:21.409
-Well, yes…
-Okay.

01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:25.205
Then let's have dinner at Samcheong-dong.

01:00:25.288 --> 01:00:26.498
Samcheong-dong?

01:00:27.749 --> 01:00:30.585
[Chan] It's a one-table restaurant
I booked before coming to Korea.

01:00:30.669 --> 01:00:32.128
Maybe it's thanks to that cloud.

01:00:32.212 --> 01:00:33.672
There was a long waitlist,

01:00:33.755 --> 01:00:36.591
but I just got a call
that someone canceled for that day.

01:00:36.675 --> 01:00:38.468
-Mmm.
-[Chan] I'll send you the link.

01:00:38.552 --> 01:00:40.053
I haven't seen this place before.

01:00:40.720 --> 01:00:42.013
[Chan] I confirmed the reservation.

01:00:42.097 --> 01:00:44.307
Ah. Mark that on your schedule.

01:00:44.391 --> 01:00:46.393
You'd better not forget or show up late.

01:00:46.476 --> 01:00:48.478
[♪ pleasant song playing]

01:00:50.105 --> 01:00:52.065
[gasps] I got distracted.

01:00:58.196 --> 01:00:59.197
[sighs]

01:01:00.574 --> 01:01:02.033
[waves splashing]

01:01:05.328 --> 01:01:07.289
[talking indistinctly]

01:01:12.586 --> 01:01:14.629
[Chan] Good morning. Did you sleep well?

01:01:15.171 --> 01:01:18.174
Our team did a sunrise shoot,
so everyone's knocked out now.

01:01:19.175 --> 01:01:20.468
Hey, a flower bloomed.

01:01:21.428 --> 01:01:24.472
But why aren't you sleeping?
Aren't you tired?

01:01:25.223 --> 01:01:26.933
[Chan] I have to enjoy every moment.

01:01:27.517 --> 01:01:30.103
Ah. There's a beautiful half-moon.

01:01:30.937 --> 01:01:32.564
Can you see it clearly in Seoul?

01:01:35.817 --> 01:01:37.444
[Haran] Yes, I can.

01:01:40.947 --> 01:01:43.366
So today's dinner is omurice.

01:01:45.785 --> 01:01:46.786
[♪ song continues]

01:01:51.708 --> 01:01:52.709
Donggu?

01:01:53.543 --> 01:01:56.296
-Hello.
-Hi. [chuckles]

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:06.431
What did you draw that character
on Donggu's uniform with?

01:02:06.514 --> 01:02:08.475
A fabric marker?

01:02:08.558 --> 01:02:09.809
-That's right. [groans]
-[gasps]

01:02:12.771 --> 01:02:13.772
[groans]

01:02:14.940 --> 01:02:17.609
Right. Mr. Park's checkup is on Wednesday.

01:02:17.692 --> 01:02:19.486
Can you check up on him?

01:02:20.487 --> 01:02:21.821
Mr. Park.

01:02:21.905 --> 01:02:23.448
Hey, you're here.

01:02:23.531 --> 01:02:24.574
Genius.

01:02:24.658 --> 01:02:25.700
-[chuckles]
-[camera shutter clicks]

01:02:26.993 --> 01:02:27.994
[♪ music fades]

01:02:28.078 --> 01:02:30.246
You didn't forget your checkup, right?

01:02:30.330 --> 01:02:33.917
There's someone
calling me every day to remind me,

01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:36.169
so I remember it
more clearly than my own birthday.

01:02:36.252 --> 01:02:37.754
[Manjae chuckles]

01:02:37.837 --> 01:02:40.256
But have you started a new hobby?

01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:42.008
You've been taking a lot of photos.

01:02:42.592 --> 01:02:45.303
Ah. Someone gave me homework,

01:02:45.387 --> 01:02:47.639
telling me to take photos
of what makes me happy.

01:02:47.722 --> 01:02:50.684
Mmm. So what did you take photos of?

01:02:50.767 --> 01:02:52.352
Nothing special.

01:02:52.435 --> 01:02:54.062
Just people around me,

01:02:54.145 --> 01:02:57.357
the moon, delicious food,

01:02:57.440 --> 01:02:59.025
that flower… Things like that.

01:02:59.109 --> 01:03:00.485
Oh.

01:03:00.568 --> 01:03:03.613
[sighs] I'm so curious how they'll look.
[chuckles softly]

01:03:03.697 --> 01:03:07.242
They say happiness is always there,
but you just miss it,

01:03:07.867 --> 01:03:11.287
so it belongs to the person
who discovers it.

01:03:11.371 --> 01:03:12.497
I guess it's true.

01:03:13.331 --> 01:03:15.542
I went on a walk with Genius earlier,

01:03:16.126 --> 01:03:18.169
and the sky was so beautiful.

01:03:18.253 --> 01:03:20.130
But no one even looked up.

01:03:20.880 --> 01:03:24.759
They were all walking around,
staring at their phones.

01:03:24.843 --> 01:03:25.844
[chuckles]

01:03:27.429 --> 01:03:29.431
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

01:03:40.859 --> 01:03:42.444
[Manjae] I have a feeling

01:03:42.527 --> 01:03:45.405
that the person who gave you that camera…

01:03:45.488 --> 01:03:46.489
[Chan inhales sharply]

01:03:46.573 --> 01:03:49.284
[Manjae] ...is someone who knows
how to look up at the sky

01:03:49.367 --> 01:03:51.036
on days like this.

01:03:52.746 --> 01:03:55.623
I guess that's why
they gave you that homework.

01:03:56.332 --> 01:04:01.504
So you can discover nice things every day,
no matter how trivial they are.

01:04:01.588 --> 01:04:05.467
They probably wanted you
to smile at least once while doing so.

01:04:05.550 --> 01:04:07.844
Isn't that right? [chuckles]

01:04:14.601 --> 01:04:16.603
Mr. Park, I think I get it now.

01:04:17.062 --> 01:04:18.063
What?

01:04:18.146 --> 01:04:21.858
I was surprised at how different I was
these days, but I didn't know why.

01:04:21.941 --> 01:04:25.612
I guess that's because
it's been such a long time since I saw it.

01:04:26.529 --> 01:04:28.406
Saw what?

01:04:29.866 --> 01:04:30.950
Myself.

01:04:33.078 --> 01:04:35.789
My past self.

01:04:36.456 --> 01:04:37.499
[♪ music continues]

01:04:37.582 --> 01:04:38.750
[Chan exclaims]

01:04:38.833 --> 01:04:40.627
[Haran chuckles]

01:04:40.710 --> 01:04:43.671
I used to be able to find happiness
in the smallest things.

01:04:43.755 --> 01:04:44.923
[exclaims nervously]

01:04:45.006 --> 01:04:47.592
It's been a while since I saw
that side of me.

01:04:47.675 --> 01:04:50.804
[laughing, exclaiming]

01:04:50.887 --> 01:04:53.765
I was able to see it again
thanks to someone.

01:04:54.724 --> 01:04:56.434
I guess that's why I was surprised.

01:05:00.688 --> 01:05:02.774
Mmm. [chuckles]

01:05:04.317 --> 01:05:05.485
Oh, my.

01:05:06.444 --> 01:05:09.322
The moon is beautiful.

01:05:09.405 --> 01:05:10.406
[sighs contentedly]

01:05:11.157 --> 01:05:13.034
I hope I can see a full moon soon.

01:05:14.285 --> 01:05:15.495
[Manjae chuckles]

01:05:18.832 --> 01:05:19.833
[sighs]

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:26.089
-[♪ music fades]
-[camera shutter clicks]

01:05:28.299 --> 01:05:29.300
[chuckles softly]

01:05:34.013 --> 01:05:35.807
Where can I find a photo studio?

01:05:41.271 --> 01:05:43.815
[in English] Remember, we're stopping
at the rest area halfway, okay?

01:05:43.898 --> 01:05:45.024
-Okay.
-See you later, bro!

01:05:45.108 --> 01:05:46.943
-Okay. See you guys.
-Drive safely. See you.

01:05:47.026 --> 01:05:48.027
Sorry, Ben.

01:05:48.111 --> 01:05:49.154
[in Korean] Take a different car.

01:05:49.237 --> 01:05:51.239
[in English] I'm going straight to Seoul.

01:05:51.322 --> 01:05:52.866
[Ben in Korean]
But it's at least four hours.

01:05:52.949 --> 01:05:55.285
-Bye.
-Hey, don't strain yourself.

01:05:55.368 --> 01:05:56.786
I'll drive.

01:05:56.870 --> 01:05:58.705
Huh? I said I'll drive.

01:05:58.788 --> 01:06:00.915
It's fine. I'll see you in Seoul.

01:06:00.999 --> 01:06:02.834
-Hey!
-I'm fine, Ben.

01:06:02.917 --> 01:06:05.879
Seonu Chan! Drive slowly, okay?

01:06:06.546 --> 01:06:07.547
[sighs]

01:06:08.840 --> 01:06:10.592
[in English] He really
shouldn't be driving.

01:06:11.342 --> 01:06:13.344
[♪ upbeat music playing]

01:06:18.308 --> 01:06:20.101
[Chan in Korean]
I'll arrive around 6:30 p.m.

01:06:21.060 --> 01:06:22.312
Find a nice pizza place for us.

01:06:22.395 --> 01:06:23.479
[Haran] See you later.

01:06:36.951 --> 01:06:38.995
ETA
1 HOUR

01:06:40.330 --> 01:06:41.539
One hour.

01:06:42.415 --> 01:06:44.500
[engine revving]

01:06:44.584 --> 01:06:46.252
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[♪ music ends]

01:06:47.670 --> 01:06:48.755
[♪ tense music playing]

01:06:48.838 --> 01:06:51.216
[cell phone continues vibrating]

01:06:56.596 --> 01:06:57.680
[truck horn blares]

01:06:57.764 --> 01:06:58.806
-[exclaims]
-[tires screech]

01:06:58.890 --> 01:07:00.308
[cell phone vibrating]

01:07:01.267 --> 01:07:02.685
Oh? Has he arrived early?

01:07:07.023 --> 01:07:09.317
-Yes, Ms. Kim.
-[Nana] Come to my office.

01:07:10.318 --> 01:07:11.736
18:04
MS. KIM

01:07:12.820 --> 01:07:14.030
Right now?

01:07:14.906 --> 01:07:15.907
[line disconnects]

01:07:20.036 --> 01:07:21.371
Me?

01:07:21.454 --> 01:07:23.414
Yes, you. Who else?

01:07:23.498 --> 01:07:25.750
Why would you make me handle the business?

01:07:25.833 --> 01:07:28.920
I'm retiring later than planned,
and you held on longer than I thought.

01:07:29.003 --> 01:07:30.046
It's time you took over.

01:07:31.172 --> 01:07:32.799
I didn't get to go at 60 as I planned,

01:07:32.882 --> 01:07:35.134
but I'm going to retire soon
and go to France.

01:07:35.718 --> 01:07:36.719
So start preparing.

01:07:37.428 --> 01:07:39.806
No, I can't do this.

01:07:39.889 --> 01:07:43.393
I'm already overwhelmed with doing design,
and I'm not qualified…

01:07:43.476 --> 01:07:45.061
You'll develop your abilities.

01:07:45.687 --> 01:07:47.063
And that was an order, not an offer.

01:07:47.647 --> 01:07:49.023
I'm not making excuses, I--

01:07:49.107 --> 01:07:50.483
You don't have a choice.

01:07:50.566 --> 01:07:53.027
If you really can't do it, then quit.

01:07:53.111 --> 01:07:55.780
I raise people for their abilities,
not with sentiment.

01:07:55.863 --> 01:07:56.906
I'll give you…

01:07:58.449 --> 01:07:59.701
a week for that report.

01:07:59.784 --> 01:08:00.785
[sighs]

01:08:05.456 --> 01:08:06.624
[sighs heavily]

01:08:07.208 --> 01:08:08.710
This is so sudden…

01:08:10.211 --> 01:08:11.212
[gasps]

01:08:12.630 --> 01:08:14.716
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

01:08:15.383 --> 01:08:16.384
[line connects]

01:08:16.467 --> 01:08:19.178
[automation] The number you have dialed
is unavailable. Please leave--

01:08:19.262 --> 01:08:20.888
Why is it off?

01:08:22.557 --> 01:08:23.766
[sighs]

01:08:24.726 --> 01:08:26.811
Call me when you get my message.

01:08:27.562 --> 01:08:29.063
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:08:29.147 --> 01:08:32.066
-[honking]
-[Chan] I couldn't react properly…

01:08:32.650 --> 01:08:34.193
Was he driving here?

01:08:36.612 --> 01:08:39.449
-Mr. Park, did you hear from Mr. Seonu?
-Oh?

01:08:40.033 --> 01:08:42.118
I guess you haven't heard yet.

01:08:43.661 --> 01:08:44.871
I got a call.

01:08:46.497 --> 01:08:47.749
What call?

01:08:49.375 --> 01:08:51.377
[Manjae]
He suddenly had to return to America.

01:08:52.045 --> 01:08:54.088
He had to head straight to the airport,

01:08:54.630 --> 01:08:57.383
so he asked me to send
his passport through express delivery.

01:08:58.801 --> 01:09:00.762
I don't know what's going on, either.

01:09:00.845 --> 01:09:04.807
He said he'd call me again soon,
but he hasn't called.

01:09:04.891 --> 01:09:05.892
[♪ music fades]

01:09:08.311 --> 01:09:09.312
[stutters]

01:09:10.688 --> 01:09:11.814
What…

01:09:12.899 --> 01:09:15.234
-I…
-[Manjae] He would have left already.

01:09:16.361 --> 01:09:19.989
He said he'd take
the earliest flight to the US.

01:09:20.073 --> 01:09:22.158
He must be gone already.

01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:25.036
[sighs]

01:09:25.119 --> 01:09:27.121
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:09:36.422 --> 01:09:38.883
MISSED CALL
ANIMATOR SEONU CHAN

01:09:42.637 --> 01:09:43.846
[sighs softly]

01:09:44.847 --> 01:09:46.057
[cell phone buzzes]

01:09:46.140 --> 01:09:47.934
YOUR PHOTOS ARE READY FOR PICKUP

01:09:48.017 --> 01:09:49.102
HOBAK PHOTO STUDIO

01:10:18.631 --> 01:10:21.217
What? He said there were 10 shots.

01:10:22.760 --> 01:10:23.928
He was lying. [sighs]

01:10:26.597 --> 01:10:27.598
[sighs]

01:10:49.829 --> 01:10:50.830
[♪ song ends]

01:10:53.291 --> 01:10:54.751
Keep enjoying your life

01:10:55.168 --> 01:10:58.004
even when… I'm not here later.

01:11:08.556 --> 01:11:10.558
[♪ uplifting song playing]

01:11:19.817 --> 01:11:21.736
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:11:45.843 --> 01:11:47.428
[Hayeong] They are all gone?

01:11:47.512 --> 01:11:50.598
[Haran] What kind of trial ends like this?

01:11:50.681 --> 01:11:53.392
-[nurse] Ms. Kim!
-[Manjae] Why did you go to the hospital?

01:11:53.476 --> 01:11:55.019
Are you sick?

01:11:55.102 --> 01:11:56.521
[Nana] I just want to walk for a bit.

01:11:56.604 --> 01:11:59.232
[Hayeong] Chan was such a nice guy.

01:11:59.315 --> 01:12:01.984
[Haran] When we first met,

01:12:02.068 --> 01:12:04.695
he said I looked like
someone trapped in winter.

01:12:04.779 --> 01:12:07.323
[Hayeong] You're not worried about Haran?

01:12:07.406 --> 01:12:08.991
[Nana] Do you regret it?

01:12:09.075 --> 01:12:12.328
Do you regret getting close to Seonu Chan?

01:12:12.912 --> 01:12:14.789
[Haran] Yes, I do.

01:12:18.251 --> 01:12:19.252
[♪ song fades]

01:12:19.335 --> 01:12:21.337
[♪ theme music playing]

01:12:27.218 --> 01:12:28.219
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:12:28.302 --> 01:12:29.303
Translated by Juyoung Park
